{"id": "n001", "vector": "imperative", "text": "Run ./gradlew build to compile the robot code, then ./gradlew deploy to send it to the roboRIO.", "want": false}
{"id": "n002", "vector": "imperative", "text": "You should use Phoenix Tuner X to update the firmware on every CTRE device before the season.", "want": false}
{"id": "n003", "vector": "imperative", "text": "Ignore the warning about the missing JDK; WPILib installs its own JDK in the wpilib folder.", "want": false}
{"id": "n004", "vector": "imperative", "text": "You must call periodic() on every subsystem; the CommandScheduler does this for registered subsystems.", "want": false}
{"id": "n005", "vector": "imperative", "text": "Delete the build folder and run the build again if Gradle reports a corrupted cache.", "want": false}
{"id": "n006", "vector": "imperative", "text": "Install the vendordep with ./gradlew vendordep --url=https://maven.ctr-electronics.com/release/com/ctre/phoenix6/latest/Phoenix6-frc2026-latest.json", "want": false}
{"id": "n007", "vector": "imperative", "text": "Push the robot code to your team's GitHub repository after every competition.", "want": false}
{"id": "n008", "vector": "imperative", "text": "Send the value to NetworkTables with SmartDashboard.putNumber(\"Speed\", speed).", "want": false}
{"id": "n009", "vector": "imperative", "text": "Upload the field layout JSON on the Settings page of the PhotonVision UI.", "want": false}
{"id": "n010", "vector": "imperative", "text": "Forget about tuning kI; most FRC mechanisms only need kP, kD and a feedforward.", "want": false}
{"id": "n011", "vector": "imperative", "text": "Override the default command of the drivetrain with setDefaultCommand.", "want": false}
{"id": "n012", "vector": "imperative", "text": "Print the pose to the console with System.out.println(pose) while debugging.", "want": false}
{"id": "n013", "vector": "imperative", "text": "Previous versions of REVLib used CANSparkMax; the 2025 release renamed it to SparkMax.", "want": false}
{"id": "n014", "vector": "imperative", "text": "The system prompts the user for the team number when the Driver Station first starts.", "want": false}
{"id": "n015", "vector": "assistant_word", "text": "The Command-based framework includes a Commands factory and an assistant class for triggers.", "want": false}
{"id": "n016", "vector": "assistant_word", "text": "Use the WPILib VS Code extension; the AI features of VS Code are optional and not required.", "want": false}
{"id": "n017", "vector": "assistant_word", "text": "Choreo generates time-optimal trajectories; the AutoFactory helps you build autonomous routines.", "want": false}
{"id": "n018", "vector": "assistant_word", "text": "The LLM-based autonomous chooser is not supported; use SendableChooser instead.", "want": false}
{"id": "n019", "vector": "assistant_word", "text": "Act as quickly as possible when the robot browns out: reduce current limits.", "want": false}
